00:13:33.033 --> 00:13:36.200
It's that people die
every day in the streets

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:39.347
and it's nothing. Walked by
dead bodies all the time.

00:13:39.347 --> 00:13:41.420
Before people even realize they're dead

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.140
and it don't even phase me anymore.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.273
I'm like that sucks.

00:13:49.026 --> 00:13:50.090
That's the kind of life it is.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:52.303
- [Mark] Your Mom and
stepdad are still alive?

00:13:54.025 --> 00:13:55.460
- Father no.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:58.886
Mother, I'm not sure I don't
stay in contact with her.

00:13:58.886 --> 00:14:00.425
- [Mark] You haven't talked to her?

00:14:00.425 --> 00:14:01.730
- Nope I don't have
anything to say to her.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.373
- [Mark] So, no family, no friends?

00:14:04.657 --> 00:14:05.523
- Pretty much.

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:13.203
Just trying to get by.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.863
Trying to have

00:14:16.863 --> 00:14:19.193
the best life I can for somebody like me.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.850
Kind of hard to have a boyfriend Whenever.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.790
All you do is have sex for money.

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:29.290
So then when they're they
want to have sexual life

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:33.660
and kind of makes them
feel some type of way. So

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.267
- [Mark] Have you been in love before?

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.073
- Yeah. Worst mistake in my life.

00:14:48.279 --> 00:14:50.500
He seen me flip out.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:52.090
I was high and tweaking.

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:52.960
He tried to restrain me

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.870
and I gave him no choice, but to hit me.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:00.610
But, but because I pushed him
to that point, he walked away.

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:02.210
He would never talk to me again.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.230
That's whenever you learn,

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.540
you can't have both worlds.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.490
You can't have a boyfriend and do this.

00:15:12.121 --> 00:15:13.893
You can't do this and have any

00:15:13.893 --> 00:15:17.480
any expectancy at a normal life.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:18.740
There isn't one because the second

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:20.910
somebody finds out what you do,

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:22.780
they see you completely differently

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:24.853
than the person they knew you to be.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.560
That one little thing, changes everything.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:30.980
All of a sudden, they don't want to hang

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:32.030
out with you because they don't know

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.000
if they can trust their
boyfriend around you

00:15:35.012 --> 00:15:36.150
or it's not even like that,

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:38.820
but that's worldview on it.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:40.857
So that's how it goes.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:45.603
Kind of hard to keep friends that way too.

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.890
- [Mark] Do you see the,
the connection between

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.750
what happened to you as a as a young girl

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:58.640
and in the situation you're in today?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.309
- Yes.

00:16:00.309 --> 00:16:01.869
- [Mark] And it's almost
like you're, you're,

00:16:01.869 --> 00:16:05.523
what you believe you deserve
is set at that young age.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:10.410
- I don't think it's so much
weight you think you deserve

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.170
because obviously I
went and ran away at 16.

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.652
If I thought I deserved that, but just

00:16:15.652 --> 00:16:18.860
because you think you
can make it on your own

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:20.883
at such a young age, you can't.

00:16:22.446 --> 00:16:24.640
So all it did is keep the cycle going

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:30.580
because I never knew anything
better than what I've got.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:35.403
So I mean it's life,

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:39.350
but sometimes I sit in wonder like

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.380
if I had come from a good family,

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:45.040
you know, or been raised
right. Or had, you know,

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:49.110
finished high school or
went to college or, you know

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.163
had the family like the
good side of family life.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.730
I wonder if I'd actually
have this kind of life.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:57.870
I don't, I mean, I guess it's possible

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.403
but I really don't see it.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.470
If you come from a good family

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.040
Why are you going to
make stupid decisions?

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.750
Not so much that running away was stupid

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.760
because I was getting beaten, but...

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:16.480
And then sometimes you sit
there and you dream like,

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.390
Oh maybe one day I'll
meet one of these dates

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.920
and they're just going to be, you know

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.970
the guy that gets me the fuck outta here.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:25.663
Still waiting.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:29.773
- [Mark] All right, Courtney.

00:17:29.773 --> 00:17:31.460
Well, thank you so much
for sharing your story

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:33.480
and I hope you figure out a way.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.313
- Thank you.

00:17:34.313 --> 00:17:35.740
- [Mark] Off the streets.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.030
- Thanks.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.717
- [Mark] Thank you very much.

00:17:38.717 --> 00:17:39.884
- No problem.

